hypotheses.statement:
For a smooth field $V=(w,z)$ on $[a,c]$, $$\label{eq:coordinate-index}
 I_{[a,c]}(V)=E_{[a,c]}(V)
       -\bigl[\langle T,\Gamma(V,V)\rangle\bigr]_a^c,$$ where $\Gamma$ denotes the Christoffel symbols in the chosen product coordinates and brackets mean final value minus initial value. In the inward coordinates at either neck boundary, if $w=0$ at that boundary, then $$\label{eq:boundary-christoffel}
 \Gamma(V,V)=\tfrac\kappa2 z_1^2\partial_\tau.$$ Thus the endpoint contribution in <a href="#eq:coordinate-index" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:coordinate-index">[eq:coordinate-index]</a> is nonnegative at an entry into or exit from the open neck, provided the interval component of the field vanishes there.

Consider a turning passage with data <a href="#eq:turn-data" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:turn-data">[eq:turn-data]</a>– <a href="#eq:turn-incidence" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:turn-incidence">[eq:turn-incidence]</a>. For every smooth field $V$ on $[0,L]$, there is a tangentially equivalent smooth field, denoted again by $V=(w,z)$, such that $$w(0)=w(L)=0,\qquad \langle V,T\rangle\ \text{is affine in }s.$$ Put $\Delta z=z(L)-z(0)$, $e=(1,0)^{\mathsf T}$, and $\mu=\kappa v_0/4>0$. For this field, $$\begin{aligned}
 I_{[0,L]}^\perp(V)
 &=E_{[0,L]}(V)+\frac{\kappa v_0}{2}
       \bigl(z_1(0)^2+z_1(L)^2\bigr)
       -\frac{(p^{\mathsf T}\Delta z)^2}{L}
       \label{eq:turning-index-identity}\\
 &\ge E_{[0,L]}(V)+\mu(e^{\mathsf T}\Delta z)^2
       -\frac{(p^{\mathsf T}\Delta z)^2}{L}.
       \label{eq:turning-index-reduction}
\end{aligned}$$ The same left side is the normal index of the original field.

For every returning passage, $$\label{eq:turning-chord}
 \int_0^L v(s)^2\,ds\le \frac{Lv_0^2}{3}.$$ If $t_*>1/4$, then $$\label{eq:turning-time-margin}
 4v_0\le\beta\kappa p_1^2L,
 \qquad \beta=\frac{1+\exp(-9/26)}{2}<1.$$

For every constant covector $q$ and every gauged field as above, $$\label{eq:turning-dual-cs}
 |q^\top X|^2\le S(q,q)E.$$ For each real $\alpha$, the boundary penalty gives the further bound $$\label{eq:turning-boundary-cs}
 |p^\top X|^2\le
 \left(S(p-\alpha e,p-\alpha e)+\frac{\alpha^2}{\mu}\right)
 \left(E+\mu(e^\top X)^2\right).$$ The smallest first factor in this inequality is $$\label{eq:turning-minimum}
 S(p,p)-\frac{S(p,e)^2}{S(e,e)+\mu^{-1}}.$$

There are constants $C_e,C_m>0$, uniform for sufficiently small $\delta>0$, such that every returning passage satisfies $$\begin{aligned}
 S(p,p)&\le L(1+v_0^2),\label{eq:turning-Spp}\\
 S(e,e)&\le C_e L,\label{eq:turning-See}\\
 |S(p,e)-Lp_1|&\le C_m\delta L|p_1|.\label{eq:turning-Spe}
\end{aligned}$$

